---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
import RouteDiagram from "../../components/RouteDiagram.astro";
---

<DocLayout
  title="Routing model"
  eyebrow="SECTION 05 / SIGNAL FLOW"
  description="Identity discovery is broad; signing is key-specific, ordered, bounded, and adaptive."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <div class="warning note">
      <strong>v0.1 DESIGN CONTRACT</strong>Main currently proxies one explicit
      upstream. Discovery, registration, adaptive ordering, and failover
      described below are being implemented before the first release.
    </div>
    <RouteDiagram />
    <h2>Candidate order</h2><ol>
      <li>
        The agent that most recently completed a signature successfully.
      </li><li>Untried forwarded and discovered sockets, newest first.</li><li>
        Explicitly configured static agents, including local 1Password.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Listing identities never promotes an agent. Only a completed signature is
      evidence that a signer is useful right now.
    </p>
    <h2>Identity requests</h2><p>
      Lanyard asks every reachable candidate, unions their public identities,
      and deduplicates equal keys. A slow or broken candidate cannot prevent
      healthy agents from contributing within the configured request budget.
    </p>
    <h2>Signature requests</h2><p>
      Only agents that advertised the requested public key are tried. A timeout
      or ordinary agent failure advances to the next matching candidate. Success
      promotes that candidate. Exhaustion returns an SSH agent failure response.
    </p>
    <h2>OpenSSH extensions</h2><p>
      <code>query</code> and <code>session-bind@openssh.com</code> are understood.
      Session bindings are replayed to candidate agents before a signature is requested,
      preserving OpenSSH’s destination-bound authentication behavior. Unknown extensions
      fail closed.
    </p>
    <table class="spec-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Budget</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead><tbody
        ><tr><td>Connect</td><td>500 ms</td></tr><tr
          ><td>Identity listing</td><td>2 s / agent</td></tr
        ><tr><td>Signing</td><td>30 s / agent</td></tr><tr
          ><td>Message size</td><td>256 KiB</td></tr
        ><tr><td>Candidates</td><td>32</td></tr></tbody
      >
    </table>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
